[i]{Silas.name} stands at one of the front windows of the building, looking outside. It's dark and fog seems to be starting to roll in, so there isn't much to see.[/i]
[i]He turns over as you walk up to him[/i]
Silas: "Hey. I was hoping I'd get to talk to you one on one for a bit."
Silas: "{FoShi.name} seems to be really scared. I was talking with him on our way back, and he would not stop talking about that monster that he saw."
- "I got that vibe too."
	Player: "I got that vibe too. He seems really shaken up."
	Silas: "I'm worried about him. He seems very serious about this monster."
- "Do you believe him?"
	Player: "Do you believe him? About the monster, I mean."
	Silas: "I get the vibe that he isn't someone who's easily shaken up. When I yelled at him last night, he was very calm about him. I believe him."
- "How do you know he's scared when you two haven't talked?"
	Player: "How do you know what he's like when he's scared if the two of you haven't talked at all?"
	Silas: "You can tell when someone is scared. It's not that difficult."
[i]{Silas.name} looks over to where {FoShi.name} sits in the lobby and sighs.[/i]
- "You're thinking this is your fault."
	Player: "You're thinking this is your fault."
